hebOCR revival (2026)
---------------------

Downloads: https://github.com/aharonium/hebocr/releases

  Windows: unzip hebocr-<version>-windows-x64.zip anywhere and run
  hebocr-gui.exe. Windows may warn that the publisher is unknown,
  because the program is not yet code-signed: choose "More info", then
  "Run anyway".

  macOS (Apple silicon, macOS 15 or later): open
  hebocr-<version>-macos-arm64.dmg and drag hebOCR to Applications. The
  first time, macOS refuses to open it because it is not signed by a
  registered Apple developer: open System Settings > Privacy & Security
  and click "Open Anyway". "Read Me.txt" in the disk image explains.

  Linux: download hebocr-<version>-x86_64.AppImage, make it executable
  (chmod +x, or Properties > Permissions in your file manager) and run
  it. It needs a distribution at least as new as Ubuntu 24.04 (glibc
  2.39). The command-line engine is inside it: run the AppImage with
  --appimage-extract and use squashfs-root/usr/bin/hebocr.

This branch ("revival") continues development of hebOCR from the 0.11
branch, with fixes merged from libhocr 0.10.18 (Dec 2013), a series of
memory-safety fixes, PNG/JPEG input, and a CMake build that also works
on Windows. Windows and Linux builds are produced automatically by
GitHub Actions: see the Actions tab of
https://github.com/aharonium/hebocr

Building with CMake:

  cmake -S . -B build
  cmake --build build
  ctest --test-dir build        (runs regression tests)

Requires GLib 2 for the command-line tool; libtiff is optional.
On Windows, build in an MSYS2 UCRT64 shell with the packages listed in
.github/workflows/build.yml.

Original README follows.

hebOCR is a free Hebrew OCR (optical character recognition) library based on the
hebocr c/c++ library originally written by Dr. by Kobi Zamir. The aim of this
project is to develop a fully open-source and free OCR (or hebrew definition)


Official downloads are available at http://code.google.com/p/hebocr/downloads/list
Full code is available using mercrial:

hg clone https://hebocr.googlecode.com/hg/ hebocr

If you want to submit code, contact me via my email and I will give you
permissions to the repository.

This library is a fork of libhocr. The fork was done since the library was
not really maintained, and the rename was done due to Google's HOCR tools
project. See:

	http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/HOCR
	http://code.google.com/p/hocr-tools/

Diego, diegoiast@gmail.com

